<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#shehu-of-borno">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shehu of Borno</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shehu of Borno is the title of the rulers of Borno in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a> from the al-Kanemi dynasty, founded by the scholar Muhammad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-amin">al-Amin</a> al-Kanemi in the early 19th century. The shehus replaced the old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sayfawa-dynasty">Sayfawa</a> kings in 1846, and since British rule they have ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maiduguri">Maiduguri</a> as one of the most senior traditional rulers in Nigeria.</p></div>
